    "ls|LS17_S5_U_106": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 106 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 2ND FEBRUARY, 2021/ MAGHA 13, 1942 (SAKA) \n \nDEATH OF FARMERS DURING PROTESTS \n \n106.  ADV. ADOOR PRAKASH: \nSHRI V.K.SREEKANDAN: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware that many farmers have lost their lives \nduring the farmers‘ agitation; \n \n(b) if so, the number of farmers who lost their lives during the agitation; \n \n(c) whether the Government has provided any compensation to the victim‘s \nfamily; \n \n(d) whether the Government has any evidence regarding infiltration of \nterrorist outfits in the agitation; and \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof and the action taken by the Government \nthereon? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI NITYANAND RAI) \n \n \n(a) to (e):  ‘Police’ and ‘Public Order’ are State subjects as per Seventh \nSchedule to the Constitution of India. The responsibilities of maintaining law \nand order, including investigation, registration / prosecution of crimes, \nconviction of accused, protection of life and property etc. rests primarily with \nthe respective State Governments. Central Government keeps a constant \nwatch on activities of individuals and organisations having bearing on \nnational security and public order through its security and law enforcement \nagencies.  Requisite action is taken as per law, whenever necessary.  \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_107": " \n \nGovernment of India \nMinistry of Consumer Affairs, Food and Public Distribution \nDepartment of Consumer Affairs \n \nLOK  SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *107 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 09.02.2021 \n \n \nFOOD INFLATION \n \n*107.  MS. RAMYA HARIDAS:  \n \nWill the Minister of CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \nmiHkksDrk ekeys] [kk| vkSj lkoZtfud forj.k ea=h be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether it is a fact that the retail food inflation has increased in the last few months;  \n(b) if so, whether the Government mechanism has not been able to control the inflation;  \n(c) whether any survey has been conducted to find out the reasons for the said inflation and if so, \nthe details thereof; and  \n(d)  the details of the hurdles being faced i n controlling the increasing prices of essential food \ncommodities?  \n \n \nANSWER \n \nmiHkksDrk ekeys] [kk| vkSj lkoZtfud forj.k ea=h  \n¼Jh ih;w’k xks;y½ \n \nTHE MINISTER OF  \nCONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n  (SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n \n(a) to (d)  :   A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n \n***** \n  \n\n \n \n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO  (d) OF LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO.*107 FOR 09.02.2021 REGARDING FOOD INFLATION. \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- \n \n(a)    :   No, Sir. Retail food inflation , as per Consumer Food Price Index (CFPI) brought out by \nthe Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation (MoSPI), has declined from 11.73 per cent \nin April, 2020 to 3.41 per cent in December, 2020. \n \n(b)         :  Does not arise. \n \n(c) & (d) : The Department of Consumer Affairs monitors the retail and wholesale prices of essential \nfood commodities reported on daily basis by State Food and Civil Supply Departments from 122 \nprice reporting centres across the country. Prices of food commodities are affected by diverse factors \nsuch as production, seasonality in crop arrivals, supply chain logistics, adverse weather conditions \netc. The daily report of prices and indicative price trends are duly analysed for taking appropriate \ndecisions for release of stocks from the buffer, export-import policy etc.  \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_108": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 108 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 2ND FEBRUARY, 2021/ MAGHA 13, 1942 (SAKA) \n \nUNAUTHORISED ELECTRONIC SURVEILLANCE \n \n108.  DR. T. SUMATHY (a) THAMIZHACHI THANGAPANDIAN: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) the number of instances of unauthorized physical/electronic surveillance \nthat have taken place in the country during the past five years; \n \n(b) the details of victims or subjects of these unauthorized electronic \nsurveillance along with their professions; \n \n(c) the details of the districts where such acts of unauthorized \nphysical/electronic surveillance were committed and the districts where the \nsubjects or victims of unauthorized physical/electronic surveillance were \nlocated; \n \n(d) the status of investigation in respect of all the instances of unauthorized \nphysical/electronic surveillance; and \n \n(e) the steps taken by the Government to curb the menace of such \nunauthorized electronic surveillance? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS  \n(SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n \n(a) to (e):  Lawful interception and monitoring can be done by the Law \nEnforcement Agencies only after obtaining approval of the  competent \nauthority in the Central or State Governments as the case may be, under the \nprovisions of section 5(2) of the Indian Telegraph Act, 1885 read with Rule  \n \n\n-2- \nL.S.US.Q NO. 108 FOR 02.02.2021   \n419A  of I ndian Telegraph  (Amendment)  Rules, 2014  and  Section 69 of the  \nInformation Technology Act, 2000 read with the  Information Technology \n(Procedure and Safeguards for interception, Monitoring and Decryption of \nInformation) Rules, 2009.  \n \nUnlawful / unauthorized interception is a punishable offence under section \n25 & 26 of the Indian Telegraph Act, 1885, with imprisonment for a term \nwhich may extend up to three years, or with fine, or with both. Police and \npublic order are State subjects as per the Seventh Schedule of the \nConstitution and the States are responsible for prevention, detection and \ninvestigation of such crime through their law enforcement machinery. \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_109": "ORIGINAL IN HINDI\nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINTSTRY OF CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION\nDEPARTMENT OF FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED OUESTION NO.'I 09\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 9ti Februaryr20.21\nt*t09. sHRl AJAY NISHAD:\nWill the Minister of CONSUMER AFFAIRS' FOOD AND PUBLIC\nDISTRIBUTIoN 5trelt+.cll errd, ureiu gt{ grffi{, kfl\"I d* be pleased to\nstate:\n(a) the details of the food subsidy on various items provided to the\nBelow Poverty Line (BPL) families and Above Poverty Line (APL)\nfamilies separatety in the country during each of the last two years;\n(b) whether the Government proposes to increase subsidy for BPL\nfamilies during the next financial year;\n(c) if so, the details thereofl and\n(d) the prices of the subsidised items being provided to States for\ndistribution during each of the tast two years and the current year?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, GOMMERGE & INDUSTRY AND\nGONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIG DISTRIBUTION\n(SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL)\n(a) to (d): A statement is laid on the Table of the House'\nFOOD SUBSIDY FOR BPL AND APL FAMILIES",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_11": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING  \nDEPARTMENT OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 11 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02.02.2021 \n \n                  DEVELOPMENT OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY IN KARNATAKA  \n \n*11. SHRI G.M. SIDDESHWAR: \n \nWill the Minister of FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING       \nमात्स्यिकी, पशुपालन और डेिरी मंत्री \nbe pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Union Government is providing any financial assistance for the various \nprojects in connection with the development of animal husbandry in Karnataka;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof during the last three years; and  \n \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING  \n                                    (SHRI GIRIRAJ SINGH) \n \n  \n (a) to (c) A Statement is laid on the table of the house. \n \n \n***** \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY OF LOK SABHA QUESTION NO. *11 \nPART (A) TO (C ) FOR ANSWER ON 02.02.2021 ASKED BY SHRI G.M. \nSIDDESHWAR, REGARDING “DEVELOPMENT OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY IN \nKARNATAKA”. \n \n \n(a) Yes, Sir.  \n \n(b) The details of financial assistance provided to Karnataka under the various schemes \nbeing implemented by Government of India for the development of animal husbandry \nin Karnataka during the last three years are as under: \n \nFund Released to the State Government of Karnataka during the last three \nyears \n(Rs. In lakh) \nS. \nNo. \nName of the scheme Years \n2017-18 2018-19 2019-20 \n1. Rashtriya Gokul Mission 857.00 164.38 756.47 \n2. National Programme for \nDairy Development  260.00 1011.00 2018.00 \n3. National Livestock \nMission 310.10 169.93 919.30 \n4. Livestock Health & \nDisease Control 1646.00 1931.42 2977.34 \n \nDairy Processing and Infrastructure Development Fund (DIDF) (as on 30.11.2020)  \n (Rs in crore)  \nNo of \nProjects \nProject Cost Loan disbursed \nTotal Loan 2018-\n19 \n2019-\n20 \n2020-\n21 Total \n8 1626.39 931.37  396.15 227.31 69.114 692.574 \n \n (c) Does not arise. \n \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_110": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK  SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 110  \n  ANSWERED ON 02.02.2021 \n  \nSCHEMES FOR RURAL AREAS \n \n110.  SHRI ANNASAHEB SHANKAR JOLLE: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the schemes available along with the funds pro vided for the Rural areas to make \nthem self-sufficient; \n(b)  whether the funds allocated were utilised duri ng the last five years; and \n(c)  if so, the details thereof and if not, the rea sons therefor? \n \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR) \n \n(a) to (c)  Ministry of Rural Development plays an important role for development of rural areas \nthrough employment generation, strengthening of liv elihood opportunities, promoting self-\nemployment, skilling of rural youths, provision of social assistance, infrastructure development, \nhousing facilities etc. The Ministry is implementin g Mahatma Gandhi National Rural \nEmployment Guarantee Scheme (MGNREGS), Deendayal An tyodaya Yojana – National Rural \nLivelihoods Mission (DAY-NRLM), Deen Dayal Upadhyay – Gramin Kaushalya Yojana (DDU-\nGKY), Pradhan Mantri Awaas Yojana – Gramin (PMAY-G) , Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak \nYojana (PMGSY), Shyama Prasad Mukherjee RURBAN Mission (SPMRM) and National Social \nAssistance Programme (NSAP). The funds allocated fo r rural development schemes are almost \nfully utilized by the Government. Details of Budget  Allocation (Revised Estimate - RE) and \nExpenditure in respect of Rural Development Schemes  for last 5 years is enclosed at    \nAnnexure-1.  \n  \n*****  \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nAnnexure -1 \n \nAnnexure referred in statement in reply to part (a) to (c) of Lok Sabha Question No. 110 due for answer on 02.02.2021 regarding \nthe funds allocated and expenditure incurred under the Scheme of Department of Rural Development durin g financial year \n2015-16 to 2020-21.  \