    "ls|LS17_S5_U_140": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 140 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 10.02.2021 \n \nFACILITIES AT KISHANGARH RAILWAY STATION \n \n †*140.  SHRI BHAGIRATH CHOUDHARY: \n \n             Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether Kishangarh, Ajmer railway station started working in a \nnew complex on 15th December, 2017;  \n \n(b) if so, the month -wise income of the station during one year before \n15th December, 2017 and one year thereafter including the month -wise \ndecline therein, if any; \n \n(c) whether a provision for two new escalators and lifts was made in \nthe Budget 2018-19 for this complex, if so, the details thereof; \n \n(d) whether the above funds were allegedly diverted to another railway \nstation, if so, the facts and also the reasons therefor; \n \n(e) whether the Government propose to urgently set up the escalators \nsanctioned in the past in view of the problems being faced by women, \ndivyangs, old age persons and children in climbing the steep stairs of \nthe gigantic foot over bridge located at this railway station complex; \nand  \n \n(f) if so, by when and if not, the reasons therefor? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMERCE & INDUSTRY AND \nCONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n \n(SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n(a)  to (f):  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n***** \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (f) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 140  BY SHRI BHAGIRATH CHOUDHARY TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 10.02.2021 REGARDING FACILITIES AT \nKISHANGARH RAILWAY STATION \n(a): Yes, Sir.   \n(b): The month-wise revenue details of Kishangarh station during one year \nbefore 15 th December, 2017 and one year thereafter along with percentag e \nvariation are as under:  \nMonth Revenue(D) Month Revenue(D) % Variation \nDec-16 24219931 Dec-17 24914781 2.87 \nJan-17 25088381 Jan-18 24731003 -1.42 \nFeb-17 25459804 Feb-18 22158283 -12.97 \nMar-17 26082748 Mar-18 25310491 -2.96 \nApr-17 24677091 Apr-18 23589469 -4.41 \nMay-17 29967341 May-18 28130881 -6.13 \nJun-17 29756743 Jun-18 24401499 -18.00 \nJul-17 27316405 Jul-18 26576179 -2.71 \nAug-17 26722993 Aug-18 24585504 -8.00 \nSep-17 24698179 Sep-18 25462367 3.09 \nOct-17 23882526 Oct-18 22739204 -4.79 \nNov-17 24343057 Nov-18 21880379 -10.12 \nTotal 312215199  294480040 -5.68 \n \n(c): Yes, Sir. Two (2) escalators and one (1) lift were sanctioned for \nKishangarh Railway station in Law Book for year 2017 -18 and reflected at \nitem no. 782 of Law Book 2018-19. \n(d) to  (f): As per policy for provision of escalators at Railway stations, \nminimum required daily footfall for provision of escalator is 25,000.  \nKishangarh Railway station does not qualify for provision of escalators at \nthis stage, hence the two escalators were  diverted to another railway \nstation.  However, provision of passenger amenities at railway stations is a \ncontinuous and on -going process depending upon need, volume of \npassenger traffic and inter-se priority, subject to availability of funds. \n\n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_141": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 141 \nANSWERED ON 11THFEBRUARY, 2021 \n \nRAIL OVER BRIDGE/FLYOVER IN WARDHA \n \n*141 SHRI RAMDAS C. TADAS: \n  \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \n \nbe pleased to state:  \n \n \n(a)  whether the construction work of Acharya Vinoba  Bhave rail over \nbridge/flyover in Wardha City of Vidarbha region has been stopped; \n \n  (b)  if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(c)  the reasons therefor  and the time by which the sanctioned work is \nlikely to be started; and  \n \n(d)  the steps being taken to complete the work on the said project in the \nstipulated time frame? \n \n \nANSWER \n \n \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n \n (a) to (d) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 141 FOR ANSWER ON 11.02.2021 \nASKED BY SHRI RAMDAS C TADAS REGARDING RAIL OVER \nBRIDGE/FLYOVER IN WARDHA \n \n \n(a) to (d) The work of Acharya VinobaBhave rail over bridge/flyover in \nWardha City of Vidarbha region is on State Highway No. 267, the \nconstruction/completion of which is the responsibility of State \nGovernment  of Maharastra. This Ministry provides grant to the State \nGovernment for the projects identified by them under Central Road \nInfrastructure Fund (CRIF)  scheme.  For this project, Ministry has \nsanctioned a grant of Rs. 45 Cr under CRIF scheme. \n  \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_142": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 142 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON FEBRUARY 11, 2021 \nREGIONAL PLAN, 2041 \nNO. 142.  SHRI KOTHA PRABHAKAR REDDY: \n            SHRI PASUNOORI DAYAKAR: \nWill the Minster of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be pl eased \nto state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government is working on Regional Plan,  \n2041; and \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof including the progress m ade, \nfunds estimated and the cost of such identified pro jects \nso far, State-wise including Andhra Pradesh and \nTelangana cities/towns? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n(SHRI  HARDEEP SINGH PURI) \n \n(a)  & (b)  A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n***** \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 142* REGARDING REGIONAL \nPLAN, 2041 FOR ANSWER ON FEBRUARY 11, 2021 \n \n(a)&(b):  The preparation of Regional Plan comes wi thin \nthe purview of state Governments. However, \nRegional Plan for the National Capital Region \n(NCR), an identified area of 55,083 square km in \nthe state of Delhi, Uttar Pradesh, Haryana and \nRajasthan is prepared by  National Capital Region \nPlanning Board (NCRPB) under the NCRPB Act, \n1985. Since the Regional Plan 2041 for NCR is at \na draft stage, it is not possible to estimate the \ncost of projects and funds needed therefor.  \n \n \n       ******  ",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_143": "O.I.H.\n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n143\n                     \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE  \n2\nND \nFEBRUARY\n,\n \n20\n2\n1\n \n \nINELIGIBLE PM\n-\nKISAN \nPAYMENTS\n \n \n143. \n \nSHRI DULAL CHAND GOSWAMI: \n \nSHRI SANGAM LAL GUPTA: \n \nSHRI DUSHYANT SINGH: \n \nSHRI RAMDAS C. TADAS: \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \n\u0000कसान \nक\u0000याण \nमं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n \n \n(a) \n \nthe\n \namount of funds disbursed under Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi (PM\n-\nKISAN) Scheme along with the number of beneficiaries of the Scheme, State\n-\nwise;\n \n \n(b) \n \nwhether undeserving beneficiaries have received payment from PM\n-\nKISAN transfers \nand these categorie\ns are ‘ineligible farmers’ and ‘income\n-\ntax payee farmers’, while eligible \nfarmers have been left out; \n \n \n(c) \n \nif so, the reasons for such disbursal of funds along with the details of the amount \ndisbursed to such beneficiaries; \n \n \n(d)\n \n \nthe States to which suc\nh ineligible beneficiaries belong along with the number of \ndetails of the number of beneficiaries in such a state; \n \n \n(e) \n \nthe steps taken by the Government to rescind such a transfer and the amount of \nmoney that has been recovered by the Government; and \n \n \n(f) \n \nthe number of farmers of Katihar Parliamentary constituency in Bihar, Pratapgarh \nParliamentary constituency of Uttar Pradesh and Wardha, Amravati and Nagpur of \nMaharashtra benefited under the Scheme and the number of people still deprived of the \nbenef\nits of this scheme?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \n\u0000कसान \nक\u0000याण \nमं\u0000ी\n  \n   \n       \n( SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR)\n  \n \n(a)\n:\n \nT\nhe amount of funds disbursed under Pradhan Mantri\n \nKisan\n \nSamman\n \nNidhi\n \n(PM\n-\nKISAN) Scheme along with the number of beneficiaries of the Scheme, State\n-\nwise as on \n22.01.2021 is placed at \nAnnexure\n-\nI\n.\n \n \nContd…2/\n-\n \n \n  \n\n \n-\n2\n-\n \n \n \n(b) to (e):\n \nDuring the verification process, if it was found that an amount of Rs.2326.8846 \ncrore\n \nwas transferred to 40,48,049 ineligible beneficiaries including income tax payees.The \nstate\n-\nwise list of such beneficiaries along with the amount transferred to them and the \namount recovered is enclosed at \nAnnexure\n-\n2\n. The list was also sent to the respect\nive State \nGovernments for rectification. The Union Government has issued a Standard Operation \nGuideline to identify such underserving beneficiary and recover amount from them.\n \n \n(f):\n \nThe number of beneficiaries under the Scheme from the Districts of Katihar\n, \nPratapgarh, Warda, Amravati and Nagpur are given below:\n \n \nKatihar District , Bihar\n-\n              \n        \n1,84,505\n \nPratapgarh District, Uttar Pradesh \n–\n \n5,28,447\n \nWardha District, Maharashtra \n-\n \n        \n1,55,227\n \nAmravati District, Maharashtra \n–\n \n     \n3,23,080\n \nNagpur District, Maharashtra \n–\n \n       \n2,00,507\n \n \n \n   \nThe eligible beneficiaries are not deprived of the benefits of PM\n-\nKISAN as it is a \ncontinuous and ongoing Scheme, and as and when data of the eligible beneficiaries are \nreceived from the States, the requi\nsite amount is transferred to the account of beneficiaries \nthrough Direct Benefit Transfer.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n  \n\n \n \nAnnexure\nI\n \n \nState\n-\nwise details of funds disbursed under PM\n-\nKISAN Scheme\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nStates\n \nNo. of Beneficiaries\n \nTotal Amount   \n \n    \n(All installments)\n \nAndaman and Nicobar Islands\n \n16,806\n \n21,58,56,000\n \nAndhra Pradesh\n \n53,36,653\n \n61,01,43,08,000\