    "ls|LS17_S5_U_149": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 149\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 11.02.2021\n \n \nRELIEF PACKAGE FOR MSME SECTOR\n \n \n*149.\n \n \n \nSHRI ARVIND GANPAT SAWANT:\n \n \nWill the Minister of MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES be pleased \nto state:\n \n \n(\na\n)\n \nwhether the Government has any data of business benefit for Micro, Small \nand Medium Enterprises (MSME) Sector out of COVID\n-\n19 relief package titled \nunder Atmanirbhar Bharat Abhi\nyan; and \n \n(\nb\n)\n \nif so, the details thereof including break\n-\nup of the same, State\n-\nwise ?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \n(SHRI NITIN GADKARI)\n \n \n(a) & (b): \n \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY \nTO PART (a) & (b) OF THE LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION No. *149 FOR ANSWER ON 11.02.2021\n \n \n \n(a) & (b): \n \n \nGovernment has taken a number of initiatives within the COVID\n-\n19 \nrelief package under Atmanirbhar Bharat Abhiyan for providing impetus to the \nMicro, Small \nand Medium Enterprises (MSME) \nsector in the country. These are: \n \n \n(\ni\n)\n \nRs. 3 Lakh crore Collateral Free Automatic Loans for business, including \nMSMEs.\n \n(\nii\n)\n \nRs.20, 000 crore Subordinate Debt for Stressed MSMEs.\n \n(\niii\n)\n \nRs. 50,000 crore equity infusion through MSME Fund of Fu\nnds.\n \n(\niv\n)\n \nNew Revised criteria for classification of MSMEs. \n \n(\nv\n)\n \nNo global tenders for procurement up to Rs. 200 crores. \n \n \nState/UT wise number of beneficiaries under ‘Rs. 3 Lakh Crore Collateral \nFree Automatic Loans for business, including MSMEs’ is given at \nAnnexure\n-\nI.\n \n \nState/UT wise number of beneficiaries under ‘Subordinate Debt for Stressed \nMSMEs’ is given at \nAnnexure\n-\nII.\n \n \nState/UT wise number of MSMEs registered on the ‘Udyam Registration’ \nPortal is given at \nAnnexure\n-\nIII.\n \n \n \n \n******\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure\n-\nI\n \n \nAnnexure \nrererred to in reply to part (a) & (b) \nto the Lok Sabha Starred Question No. *149 \nfor answer on 11.02.2021\n \n \nState/UT wise number of beneficiaries under ‘Rs. 3 Lakh Crore\n \nCollateral Free Automatic \nLoans for business, including MSMEs’ as on 25\nth\n \nJanuary, 2021 \n \nState/UT\n \nNumber of \nGuarantees \n \n% Number of \nGuarantees\n \nGuarantee Amount \n(Rs. in Crore)\n \n% Guarantee \nAmount\n \nANDAMAN AND \nNICOBAR ISLANDS\n \n1885\n \n0.02%\n \n92.09\n \n0.05%\n \nANDHRA \nPRADESH\n \n246973\n \n2.69%\n \n7489.3\n \n3.72%\n \nARUNACHAL PRADESH\n \n2181\n \n0.02%\n \n62.51\n \n0.03%\n \nASSAM\n \n530121\n \n5.77%\n \n2443.6\n \n1.21%\n \nBIHAR\n \n644396\n \n7.01%\n \n3520.16\n \n1.75%\n \nCHANDIGARH\n \n6326\n \n0.07%\n \n779.5\n \n0.39%\n \nCHHATTISGARH\n \n135622\n \n1.48%\n \n3528.39\n \n1.75%\n \nDADRA AND NAGAR \nHAVELI\n \n2012\n \n0.02%\n \n170.72\n \n0.08%\n \nDAMAN AND DIU\n \n870\n \n0.01%\n \n115.86\n \n0.06%\n \nDELHI\n \n89128\n \n0.97%\n \n11814.73\n \n5.87%\n \nGOA\n \n11562\n \n0.13%\n \n631.02\n \n0.31%\n \nGUJARAT\n \n284716\n \n3.10%\n \n18996.94\n \n9.43%\n \nHARYANA\n \n154876\n \n1.69%\n \n9444.42\n \n4.69%\n \nHIMACHAL PRADESH\n \n46102\n \n0.50%\n \n1341.92\n \n0.67%\n \nJAMMU AND KASHMIR\n \n66631\n \n0.73%\n \n1841.39\n \n0.91%\n \nJHARKHAND\n \n239019\n \n2.60%\n \n2396.1\n \n1.19%\n \nKARNATAKA\n \n445454\n \n4.85%\n \n13044.81\n \n6.48%\n \nKERALA\n \n399278\n \n4.34%\n \n7075.54\n \n3.51%\n \nLADAKH\n \n994\n \n0.01%\n \n43.21\n \n0.02%\n \nLAKSHADWEEP\n \n355\n \n0.00%\n \n1.68\n \n0.00%\n \nMADHYA PRADESH\n \n373685\n \n4.07%\n \n6965.54\n \n3.46%\n \nMAHARASHTRA\n \n799050\n \n8.69%\n \n30324.22\n \n15.06%\n \nMANIPUR\n \n9880\n \n0.11%\n \n109.92\n \n0.05%\n \nMEGHALAYA\n \n11169\n \n0.12%\n \n152.97\n \n0.08%\n \nMIZORAM\n \n3653\n \n0.04%\n \n52.42\n 