    "ls|LS17_S5_U_150": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 150 \nANSWERED ON 11TH FEBRUARY, 2021 \n  \nCONVERSION OF NHS INTO FOUR AND SIX LANES \n \n*150. SHRI SUBRAT PATHAK:  \n   SHRI RAVINDRA KUSHWAHA: \n \nWILL THE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) the targets fixed for converting the National Highways in the \ncountry into four lane and six lane during the year 2019-2020, State-\nwise; \n(b) the length of each such NH which has been converted into four \nlane and six lane, separately so far, State-wise; \n(c) the length of NHs on which such conversion work is pending along \nwith the time by which it is likely to be completed; \n(d) the funds allocated by the Government to various States for this \npurpose, State-wise; and \n(e) the length of NHs in the country expected to be converted into \nfour lane and six lane in the coming three years, State-wise? \n \nANSWER \n  \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n \n(a) to (e) A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 150 ON 11TH FEBRUARY, 2021  \nASKED BY SHRI SUBRAT PATHAK, SHRI RAVIND RA KUSHWAHA  \n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� \n \n \n(a) & (b) Target for con version of National Highways into 4/6 lane \nwas 3560 km in the year 2019-20. Conversion of the targeted \nlength of National Highways into 4/6 lane was completed by \nJuly 2020. The state-wise length completed is at Annexure-I.  \n(c) During the current financial year, 3895 km is being converted \ninto 4/6 lane out of which  2300 km is completed by              \n31st January 2021.  \n(d) The details o f fund allocated and amount utilized for \ndevelopment of National Highways in the year 2020 -21 up to \nDecember 2020 are provided at Annexure-II.  \n(e)  Length of 26,865 Km is to be developed to 4/6 lane standards  \nunder Bharatmala upto December 2024. State wis e list is \nenclosed at Annexure-III.  \n \n\n                             ANNEXURE-I  \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) & (b) OF LOK  \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 150 ON 11TH FEBRUARY, 2021 \nASKED BY SHRI SUBRAT PATHAK, SHRI RAVINDRA KUSHWAHA \n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� \n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------   \nThe state-wise length of highways converted into 4/ 6 lane from \nApril 2019 to July 2020: \n \n \nSr. No. State/ UT Length in Km     \n( 4L/6L) \n1 Andhra Pradesh 190 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 2 \n3 Assam 2 \n4 Bihar 37 \n5 Chhattisgarh 31 \n6 Delhi 12 \n7 Goa 30 \n8 Gujarat 163 \n9 Haryana 49 \n10 Himachal Pradesh 33 \n11 Jammu & Kashmir  8 \n12 Jharkhand 182 \n13 Karnataka 268 \n14 Kerala 10 \n15 Madhya Pradesh 365 \n16 Maharashtra 783 \n17 Nagaland 10 \n18 Odisha 306 \n19 Punjab 69 \n20 Rajasthan 179 \n21 Tamil Nadu 103 \n22 Telangana 53 \n23 Uttar Pradesh 490 \n24 Uttarakhand 76 \n25 West Bengal 84 \n26 Expressway 25 \n Total 3560 \n\nANNEXURE-II \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART  (d) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 150 ON 11 TH FEBRUARY, 2021 ASKED BY \nSHRI SUBRAT PATHAK, SHRI RAVINDRA KUSHWAHA REGARDING \n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� \n \n \nDetails of fund allocated and amount utilized for development of \nNational Highways in the year 2020-21 \n \nSl. \nNo. States / UTs / Schemes / Agency 2020-21* \nAlloc. Expd. \n1 Andhra Pradesh 1,809 1,367 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 60 37 \n3 Assam 350 292 \n4 Bihar 1,839 1,487 \n5 Chhattisgarh 665 475 \n6 Goa 930 498 \n7 Gujarat 730 609 \n8 Haryana 160 106 \n9 Himachal Pradesh 180 120 \n11 Jharkhand 330 213 \n12 Karnataka 1,101 889 