    "ls|LS17_S5_U_158": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI,\nDEPARTMENT OF WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. †*158\nANSWERED ON 11.02.2021\nFUNDS FOR MINOR IRRIGATION PROJECTS\n†*158. SHRI ASHOK MAHADEORAO NETE\nWill the Minister of JAL SHAKTI be pleased to state:\n(a) the number of minor irrigation projects in the country sanctioned during the last three years and the\ncurrent year, particularly in Maharashtra;\n(b) the amount allocated for implementation of the said projects, State-wise including Maharashtra; and\n(c) the time by which the said irrigation projects are likely to be completed?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF JAL SHAKTI\n(SHRI GAJENDRA SINGH SHEKHAWAT)\n(a) to (c) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n*****\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO ( c) OF STARRED QUESTION\nNo. *158 TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 11.02.2021 REGARDING “ FUNDS FOR\nMINOR IRRIGATION PROJECTS” BY SHRI ASHOK MAHADEORAO NETE\n(a) to (c) Project planning, formulation, approval and implementation of minor irrigation projects are\ntaken up by the various States Governments as per their own requirement and priorities, and the role\nof Central Government is limited to providing financial assista nce under the existing schemes of\nMinistry of Jal Shakti, subject to the projects complying with the laid down guidelines of the schemes\nand availability of funds.\nPradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchayee Yojana (PMKSY) was launched in 2015 -16 with an aim to\nenhance physical access of water on farm and expand cultivable area under assured irrigation,\nimprove on farm water use efficiency, introduce sustainable water conservation practices etc.\nPMKSY- Har Khet Ko Pani (HKKP) is one of the component of PMKSY. The Sur face Minor\nIrrigation (SMI) scheme has become a part of PMKSY (HKKP) , under which Central Assistance is\nprovided by Ministry of Jal Shakti for minor irrigation projects.\nDetails regarding Surface Minor Irrigation (SMI) projects sanctioned under PMKSY -HKKP\nin the country during the last three years, and the current year, are Annexed herewith. No SMI\nproject from the State of Maharashtra has been included under PMKSY-HKKP during above period.\nFurther, in July 2018, Gov ernment of India approved a Special Package to provide Central\nAssistance of Rs.3831.41 crore to complete 83 Surface Minor Irrigation (SMI) projects and 8\nMajor/Medium Irrigation Projects in suicide prone districts in Vidarbha , Marathwada and res t of\nMaharashtra region of the S tate.The Central Assistance earmarked for the 83 SMI projects, having\nfootprints in the districts of Amravati, Akola, Washim, Yavatmal, Buldhana and Wardha from\nVidarbha region and Aurangabad, Jalna, Nanded, Latur and Beed f rom Marathwada region, is\nRs.1203.79 Crore.  These SMI Projects are scheduled to be completed in phases, upto 2022-23.\nSo far, total Central Assistance of Rs. 434.751 crore has been released to these 83 SMI\nprojects under the Special Package during 2018 -19 to 2020 -21, and irrigation potential of about\n13,000 hectares have been created, d uring 2018-19 to 20 19-20. 18 projects have been completed as\nreported by State.\n*****\n\nANNEXURE\nAnnexure referred to in reply to p art (a) to (c) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No. *158 for reply on 11.02.2021 regarding “Funds for Minor\nIrrigation Projects”.\nSl.No. Year of\nInclusion State\nNumber of\nProjects\nIncluded\nTargeted\nPotential\nCumulative\nPotential\nAchieved till\n03/2020\nEstimated\nCost\nEligible\nCentral\nShare (CA)\nCumulative\nCA released\ntill 03/2020\nCumulative\nExpenditure\ntill 03/2020\nNo of\nProjects\ncompleted\ntill 03/2020\nCA\nRelease\n2020-21\n(Rs. in\ncrore)\nCompletion\nDate\nThousand hectare Rs. in crore\n1 2017-18\nHimachal\nPradesh 111 17.881 6.108 338.18 304.37 202.36 224.84 55 51.00 March, 21\n2 Mizoram 22 1.791 0.984 28.76 25.88 12.92 15.80 0 6.48 March, 21\n3\n2018-19\nArunachal\nPradesh 604 22.766 2.700 485