    "ls|LS17_S5_U_185": " \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nGovernment of India \nMinistry of Consumer Affairs, Food and Public Distribution \nDepartment of Consumer Affairs \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.185 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02.02.2021 \n \nCONSUMER AWARENESS POLICY \n \n185. SHRI SHRIRANG APPA BARNE: SHRI SUDHEER GUPTA: SHRI SANJAY \nSADASHIVRAO MANDLIK: SHRI CHANDRA SEKHAR SAHU: SHRI MANOJ \nTIWARI: SHRI BIDYUT BARAN MAHATO:  \n \nWill the Minister of CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \nmiHkksDrk ekeys] [kk| vkSj lkoZtfud forj.k ea=h be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has implemented any policy/strategy to educate/make consumers \naware about their rights across the country particularly in rural areas and if so, the details \nthereof;  \n(b) whether the Government has sought participation of Panchayati Raj Institutions (PRIs) for \neffective implementation of the said policy/strategy in rural areas of the country;  \n(c) if so, the details thereof along with the response received from PRIs in this regard;  \n(d) whether the complaints of violation of consumer rights increased in the country during each of \nthe last three years and the current year; and  \n(e) if so, the details thereof along with the reasons for the same along with the action taken/being \ntaken on such complaints, State/UT-wise? \n \nANSWER \n \nmiHkksDrk ekeys] [kk| vkSj lkoZtfud forj.k jkT; ea=h  \n¼Jh nkuos jkolkgsc nknkjko½ \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE  \nCONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n(SHRI DANVE RAOSAHEB DADARAO) \n \n(a)      :  Yes, Sir. The Government carries out a multi-media “ Jago Grahak  Jago” campaign on \npan-India basis covering both rural and urban areas through print, electronic, outdoor and social media. \nConsumer Awareness information has been disseminated through post o ffices and Krishi Vigyan \nKendras.  Grants-in-aid are released to States/UTs for creating consumer awareness in the respective \nStates/UTs in their regional languages so as to further ensure that the campaign reaches the rural and \nbackward areas of the country.  Consumer awareness and education is also promoted through fairs and \nmelas in rural and urban areas.  \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n(b)  & (c) :       The Government has involved of PRIs in rural areas through Ministry of Panchayati \nRaj for effective implementation to educat e and make consumers aware about their rights across the \ncountry. As outreach efforts, the Ministry of Panchayati Raj disseminated consumer awareness \ninformation to Gram Panchayats and on the National Consumer Day on 24.12.2020, there was an \ninteraction with the selected Panchayats of Jharkhand. \n \n(d) & (e)   :       Details of consumer cases Filed, Disposed and Cumulative Pendency in all Consumer \nCommissions across the Country (State/UT-wise) during the year 2018-21 is given at Annexure. \n  \n*****  \n\n \nANNEXURE \n  \nANNEXURE REFERRED IN REPLY TO PARTS (d) &  (e) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 185 FOR 02.02.2021 REGARDING CONSUMER AWARENESS POLICY \n  \n  \nSTATUS OF CASES IN DISTRICT COMMISSION FOR THE YEAR 2018 \n  \nYear Commission(s) Filed  Restored Disposed  Cumulative Pending \n1.   Andhra Pradesh 1935 16 1791 160 \n2.   Arunachal Pradesh 26 0 10 16 \n3.   Assam 406 3 382 27 \n4.   Bihar 3023 1 1405 1619 \n5.   Chhattisgarh 4531 31 3509 1053 \n6.   Goa 169 10 180 0 \n7.   Gujarat 8222 133 6286 2069 \n8.   Haryana 7507 42 7392 157 \n9.   Himachal Pradesh 1411 24 1523 0 \n10.   Jammu & Kashmir 413 0 314 99 \n11.   Jharkhand 1224 4 630 598 \n12.   Karnataka 8911 119 8546 484 \n13.   Kerala 4729 92 4597 224 \n14.   Madhya Pradesh 8466 30 4022 4474 \n15.   Maharashtra 14963 152 12283 2832 \n16.   Manipur 18 0 18 0 \n17.   Meghalaya 48 1 26 23 \n18.   Mizoram 67 0 35 32 \n19.   Nagaland 12 0 0 12 \n20.   Orissa 2934 5 2170 769 \n21.   Punjab 8524 32 6100 2457 \n22.   Rajasthan 10682 75 11304 0 \n23.   Sikkim 25 0 19 6 \n24.   Tamil Nadu 2826 36 3041 0 \n25.   Telanga