    "ls|LS17_S5_U_21": "O.I.H. \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK  SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 21 \n  ANSWERED ON 02.02.2021 \n \nJOBS UNDER DDU-GKY \n \n21.  SHRI NAYAB SINGH: \nSHRI JOHN BARLA: \nSHRI HEMANT TUKARAM GODSE: \nDR. RAM SHANKAR KATHERIA: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government is running the Deen Day al Upadhyay Grameen Kaushalya \nYojana (DDU-GKY) in the country and if so, the details thereof; \n(b)  whether the rural youths are being imparted tr aining under this scheme in the \ncountry including districts of Maharashtra especially in Nashik, districts of Haryana \nespecially in Kurukshetra, districts in West Bengal  especially in Alipurduar and \ndistricts of Uttar Pradesh especially Etawa; \n(c)  if so, the details of youths provided training  till date and if not, the reasons therefor; \n(d)  whether jobs/placements have been provided to these trained youths and if so, the \ndetails thereof; and \n(e)  the percentage of trained youths who have been  provided job opportunities \nalongwith the details thereof?  \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR) \n \n \n(a)  Yes, Sir. Ministry of Rural Development is imp lementing Deen Dayal Upadhyaya Grameen \nKaushalyaYojana (DDU-GKY), a placement linked skill  development program for rural poor \nyouth under National Rural Livelihoods Mission (NRL M) since September, 2014. Rural Youth \nin the age group of 15-35 Years are covered under this scheme. There is a mandatory coverage of \nsocially disadvantaged groups, i.e for SC/ST-50%, M inorities- 15%, and Women-33% under \nDDU-GKY. \n       DDU-GKY follows a 3-tier implementation arch itecture in PPP mode, with the National \nUnit responsible for policy, funding of central sha re and technical support, State Rural \nLivelihood Missions (SRLMs)/ State Skills Missions responsible for funding of state share, \nimplementation and monitoring controls, and Project  Implementing Agencies (PIAs), mostly \nprivate training partners, responsible for mobilization, training and placements. \n\n \nUnder DDU-GKY, two special programs are being implemented: \ni.  ROSHNI program is being implemented for 27 left wing extremist affected areas of 9 States  \nwith mandatory residential course with 40% coverage to women candidates  \nii.  Himayat- All youth of the UT of Jammu & Kashmir an d Ladakh are covered under this \nscheme. \n       DDU-GKY follows a funding pattern of 60:40 b etween Centre and State generally. Funding \npattern in case 8 North Eastern States, Uttarakhand  and Himachal Pradesh is 90:10 between \nCentre and State. All UTs including UT of J&K and L adakh, receives 100% funding from \nCentre.   \n      DDU-GKY is working with 760 PIAs having 1638 Projects with 1792 Training centres \nacross the country. \nUnder DDU-GKY, a total of 10.63 lakh candidates hav e been trained and \n6.80 Lakh candidates have been placed since incepti on (September, 2014) till December, 2020.  \nYear-wise break-up of the same is given below:- \n \nYear  Total no. of candidates \ntrained under DDU-GKY  \nTotal no. of candidates placed \nunder DDU-GKY  \n2014-15 43,038 21,446  \n2015-16 2,36,471 1,09,512  \n2016-17 1,62,586 1,47,883  \n2017-18 1,31,527 75,787  \n2018-19 2,41,080 1,38,248  \n2019-20  2,38,336 1,50,199  \n2020-21(Till \nDecember 2020) 9,986 36,933  \nTotal  10,63,024 6,80,008  \n \n \n(b) to (e)  Yes Sir. DDU-GKY is being implemented i n various districts of Maharashtra \nincluding Nashik, districts of Haryana including in  Kurukshetra, districts in West Bengal  \nincluding Alipurduar and districts of Uttar Pradesh  including Etawa. The district-wise number of \ncandidates trained, placed and percentage of placem ent since 2014-15 till December, 2020 in \nMaharashtra, Haryana, West Bengal and Uttar Pradesh  is given at Annexure-1, Annexure-2, \nAnnexure-3 and Annexure-4 respectively. \n***** \n \n  \n \n\nAnnexure-1 \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY OF UNSTARRED QUESTION  NO 21 FOR \nREPLY IN LOK SABHA ON 02.02.2020   \nDistrict wise Implementation of DDU-GKY in Maharashtra \n \n S. No.  District Trained Placed Percentage of placed candid ates \n1 Ahmednagar 1460  774  53.01 \n2 Akola 798  364  45.61 \n3 Amaravati 3285  1863  56.71 \n4 Aurangabad 1224  602  49.18 \n5 Beed 1101  370  33.61 \n6 Bhandara 1983  1010  50.93 \n7 Buldhana 1116  575  51.52 \n8 Chandrapur 2123  963  45.36 \n9 Dhule 798  290  36.34 \n10 Gadchiroli 2682  1597  59.55 \n11 Gondia 2093  1050  50.17 \n12 Hingoli 844  394  46.68 \n13 Jalgaon 1039  442  42.54 \n14 Jalna 1680  781  46.49 \n15 Kolhapur 551  263  47.73 \n16 Latur 672  317  47.17 \n17 Nagpur 1953  1157  59.24 \n18 Nanded 1052  754  71.67 \n19 Nandurbar 1842  813  44.14 \n20 Nashik 2424  1115  46.00 \n21 Osmanabad 1080  374  34.63 \n22 Palghar 998  373  37.37 \n23 Parbhani 699  283  40.49 \n24 Pune 1352  683  50.52 \n25 Raigad 429  233  54.31 \n26 Ratnagiri 914  408  44.64 \n27 Sangli 294  124  42.18 \n28 Satara 1154  672  58.23 \n29 Sindhudurg 636  368  57.86 \n30 Solapur 2144  1185  55.27 \n31 Thane 645  293  45.43 \n32 Wardha 1709  929  54.36 \n33 Washim 820  490  59.76 \n34 Yavatmal 2279  1296  56.87 \n  Grand Total 45873  23205  50.59 \n\n \n Annexure-2 \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY OF UNSTARRED QUESTION  NO 21 FOR \nREPLY IN LOK SABHA ON 02.02.2020   \nDistrict wise Implementation of DDU-GKY in Haryana \n \nS. \nNo. Candidate District Trained \n Placed  Percentage of placed candidates \n1 AMBALA 1797  1018  56.6%  \n2 BHIWANI 2373  842  35.5%  \n3 FARIDABAD 979  487  49.7%  \n4 FATEHABAD 2406  1365  56.7%  \n5 GURGAON 352  33  9.4%  \n6 HISAR 3123  2130  68.2%  \n7 JHAJJAR 1064  573  53.9%  \n8 JIND 3076  1300  42.3%  \n9 KAITHAL 1707  853  50.0%  \n10  KARNAL 2616  1653  63.2%  \n11  KURUKSHETRA 2572  1570  61.0%  \n12  MAHENDRAGARH  1418  1008  71.1%  \n13  MEWAT 502  69  13.7%  \n14  PALWAL 232  78  