 \n75  VARANASI 3759  2038  54.22  \nTotal 128104  58526  45.69  \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_210": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, \nCOOPERATION\n \n& FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n210\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n \n9\nTH\n \nMARCH, 2021\n \n \nKCC UNDER ATMA NIRBHAR BHARAT PACKAGE\n \n \n*210. \n   \nSHRI DUSHYANT SINGH: \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS \nWELFARE\n  \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \nbe pleased to state\n:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the Government plans to provide Kisan Credit Card (KCC) to 2.5 crore \nfarmers under Atma Nirbhar Bharat package; \n \n \n(b) \n \nif so, the details of the number of farmers who have been given these credit cards \nunder Atma Nirbhar Bharat package, State\n-\nwise; \n \n \n(c) \n \nthe details of the amount of loan availed by farmers who have been given these cards \nunder Atma Nirbhar Bharat pac\nkage, State\n-\nwise; \n \n \n(d)\n \n \nthe size of land\n-\nholding of the farmers to whom these cards have been distributed \nunder Atma Nirbhar Bharat package; \n \n \n(e) \n \nthe number of agriculture credit agencies available in districts in which more than 50 of \nthese cards have \nbeen distributed under Atma Nirbhar Bharat package; and \n \n \n(f) \n \nwhether the target of 2.5 crore cards include the 1.5 crore dairy farmers covered under \nthe Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and Dairying and if so, the details thereof?\n \n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER\n \nOF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n \n \n  \n(SHRI NARENDRA  SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n \n(a) to (\nf\n):\n \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (\nf\n) OF L\nOK SABHA \nSTARRED \nQUESTION NO.\n  \n210\n    \nDUE FOR REPLY ON \n9\nTH\n \nMARCH, 2021\n.\n \n \n(a) to (c): \n \nYes Sir. \nUnder the Atma\n \nNirbhar\n \nBharat\n \n(ANB)\n \npackage, the target is to provide \nKCC to 2.5 crore new farmers. \nAround 1.96 crore \nKCC \nhave been \nsanctioned \nto farmers \nunder ANB package\n. The \nstate\n-\nwise \ndetails of the same are \nat\n \nAnnexure.\n  \nThe\n \ndetails of the \namount of loan availed by farmers who have been given these cards under Atma\n \nNirb\nhar \nBharat package, State\n-\nwise is not available. However, loans are availed by the farmers as \nper the KCC limit sancti\noned to them based on scale of finance for the crop under cultivation, \npost harvest/household/consumption requirements, maintenance expenses of farm assets, \nas also working capital requirement for animal husbandry, dairy and fisheries. Total amount \nof Rs. \n1.87 lakh crore credit limits has been sanctioned which works out to an average \nsanctioned limit of around 0.95 lakh per farmer.\n \n(d)\n: \n \nAll farmers irrespective of the size of land,\n \npracticing Crop Husbandry\n \n(including \nsharecroppers and tenant farmers)\n \nAnim\nal Husbandry, Dairying and Fisheries\n \nare eligible for \nKCC. \n \n(e): \n \nAll the Scheduled Commercial Banks\n \n(SCBs), Cooperative Banks\n \nand \nRegional Rural \nBanks can issue KCC to the eligible farmers. Farmers can \nalso \napply through\n \nCommon \nService Centers (CSCs)\n \nfor KCC\n.\n \n(f): \n \nThe target set under Atma\n \nNirbhar Bharat package includes farmers practicing Crop \nHusbandry, Animal Husbandry, Dairying& Fisheries. \n \n \n \n\n \nAnnexure\n \n \nKCC issued under Atma\n \nNirbhar Bharat Package as on 26\n-\n02\n-\n2021\n \nSl. No.\n \nState/UT\n \nNumber\n \n1\n \nANDAMAN AND NICOBAR ISLANDS\n \n3,237\n \n2\n \nANDHRA PRADESH\n \n1,296,853\n \n3\n \nARUNACHAL PRADESH\n \n2,204\n \n4\n \nASSAM\n \n257,555\n \n5\n \nBIHAR\n \n395,718\n \n6\n \nCHANDIGARH\n \n6,411\n \n7\n \nCHHATTISGARH\n \n223,975\n \n8\n \nDADRA AND NAGAR HAVELI\n \n208\n \n9\n \nDAMAN AND DIU\n \n789\n \n10\n \nDELHI\n \n3,364\n \n11\n \nGOA\n \n7,901\n \n12\n \nGUJARAT\n \n1,109,583\n \n13\n \nHARYANA\n \n275,219\n \n14\n \nHIMACHAL PRADESH\n \n106,863\n \n15\n \nJAMMU AND KASHMIR\n \n657,068\n \n16\n \nJHARKHAND\n \n180,231\n \n17\n \nKARNATAKA\n \n1,330,817\n \n18\n \nKERALA\n \n745,706\n \n19\n \nLADAKH\n \n5,973\n \n20\n \nLAKSHADWEEP\n \n56\n \n21\n \nMADHYA PRADESH\n \n1,356,915\n \n22\n \nMAHARASHTRA\n \n2,956,591\n \n23\n \nMANIPUR\n \n4,485\n \n24\n \nMEGHALAYA\n \n13,543\n \n25\n \nMIZORAM\n \n14,013\n \n26\n \nNAGALAND\n \n10,067\n \n27\n \nODISHA\n \n481,364\n \n28\n \nPUDUCHERRY UT\n \n7,125\n \n29\n \nPUNJAB\n \n367,681\n \n30\n \nRAJASTHAN\n \n1,693,410\n \n31\n \nSIKKIM\n \n2,546\n \n32\n \nTAMIL NADU\n \n825,191\n \n33\n \nTELENGANA\n \n860,150\n \n34\n \nTRIPURA\n \n148,764\n \n35\n \nUTTAR \nPRADESH\n \n2,402,010\n \n36\n \nUTTARAKHAND\n \n497,663\n \n37\n \nWEST BENGAL\n \n1,376,107\n \n \nTotal\n \n19,627,357\n \nSource: Reported by Public sector banks and NABARD on FI Plan Portal\n \n****\n ",
