�����������������\n�����������������\n�\n� ������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���� ������� �������� ����� ��� ��������� �������� ������ ������ ���������� ������� �������\n������������� ��������� ����� ��� ������ ������ ��������� ��� ���� ����� ���� ������ ���� �����\n������� ��������� �������� ������������� ������� ������� ������ ������� ����������� ������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n��������\n�\n\n������\n�\n�\n����������� ��������� ����� ���������� ��������� �������� ������ �������� ������� ������\n������������� ������ ��������� ������� ����������� ��������������� ��������� ���������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������� ����� ������������ ���� ���������� ������������ ������� �������� ��� ���� ��������� ���\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��� ���� ���������� ���� �������� �������� ������������ ������������� ��� ���� ����������� ��� ����\n�������� ������� ���� �������� ��� ���������� ������� �� �������� ������� ���������� ����������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��� ���� ������ ��� ������ ����� ����� �� ������ ��� ��������� ������������ ������� ������ ����\n���������������� ��� �������� �������� �������������� ���������� ���� �������� �����������\n����������������\n�\n���������\n� �\n\n�\n�",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_242": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nDEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 242\nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 12TH MARCH, 2021\nCOVID VACCINATION\n*242. SHRI G.S. BASAVARAJ:\nSHRI AJAY KUMAR MISRA TENI:\nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE be pleased to state:\n(a) present status of containment and control of COVID-19 cases including the number\nof districts where no cases have been reported over a long period of time, State/UT -\nwise;\n(b) status of COVID-19 vaccination, State/UT-wise;\n(c) whether Government proposes to speed up the vaccination process in view of rising\ncases and new strain of virus causing COVID -19, if so, the details thereof and the\naction taken in this regard including private participation in vaccination drive;\n(d) number of health care workers/frontline workers providing treatment to COVID-19\npatients, State/ UT-wise;\n(e) whether Government has achieved the target of first dose of COVID -19\nvaccination to the healthcare/ frontline workers, if so, the details thereof; and\n(f) if not, steps taken by Government to speed up vaccination of healthcare/frontline\nworkers to enable them to effectively tackle rising cases of COVID -19 and its new\nstrain?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\n(DR. HARSH VARDHAN)\n(a) to (f) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO.242* FOR 12TH MARCH, 2021\n(a) As on 8th March 2021, there are a total of 1,12,29,398 confirmed COVID -19\ncases reported by States and UTs. A total of 1,57,853 persons have died due to\nCOVID-19 in the country. A large majority of total cases (96.91%) have recovered.\nIndia’s case fatality rate of 1.41% is also lowest among similarly affected countries.\nAs of now, five States (Maharashtra, Kerala, Punjab, Karnataka, and Tamil Nadu) are\ncontributing to 83.98% of all active cases in the country, of these only 2 States (Kerala\nand Maharashtra) are contributing to almost 74.37% of all active cases in the country.\nA total of 44 districts have not reported any new case of COVID -19 for more than 28\ndays. State/UT wise details of such districts is given at Annexure-1.\n(b) As on 09 th March 2021, a total of 2.3 crore doses of COVID -19 vaccine have\nbeen administered to beneficiaries prioritized by National Expert Group on Vaccine\nAdministration for COVID -19 (NEGVAC). The State/UT -wise number of pers ons\nadministered COVID-19 vaccine is given at Annexure-2.\n(c) Government is increasing the speed of the vaccination drive by increasing the\nnumber of COVID-19 Vaccination Centres (CVCs) in Government as well as Private\nHealth Facilities.\n(d) Since ‘Health’ is a St ate responsibility, no centralized data on number of\nhealthcare workers/frontline workers providing treatment to COVID -19 patients in\neach State/UT is being maintained by Ministry of Health & Family Welfare but such\ndatabase is available with States/UTs.\n(e) & (f) COVID -19 vaccination is entirely voluntary. As on 09 th March 2021,\n80.85% of the registered Health Care Workers and 63.40% of the registered Front Line\nWorkers have received 1 st dose of COVID -19 Vaccine. Vaccination drive of these\nbeneficiaries is bei ng increased by increasing the number of COVID -19 Vaccination\nCentres (CVCs) in Government as well as Private Health Facilities, and undertaking\nvarious interventions to build up and sustain vaccine confidence through dissemination\nof factual information about the vaccine and the vaccination process.\n\nAnnexure-1\nState/UT wise districts not reported any new case of COVID-19 for more than 28 days\n(as on 8th March 2021)\nS. No. State Name District Name\n1\nArunachal Pradesh\nChanglang\n2 Dibang Valley\n3 East Kameng\n4 East Siang\n5 Kurung Kumey\n6 Lohit\n7 Lower Dibang Valley\n8 Lower Subansiri\n9 Tawang\n10 Upper Siang\n11 Upper Subansiri\n12 Anjaw\n13 Longding\n14 Kra Daadi\n15 Siang\n16 Kamle\n17 Lower Siang\n18 Pakke Kessang\n19 Leparada\n20 Shi Yomi\n21\nAssam\nBongaigaon\n22 Dhubri\n23 Hailakandi\n24 Karbi Anglong\n25 Dima Hasao\n26 Chirang\n27 Baksa\n28 Majuli\n29 Charaideo\n30 West Karbi Anglong\n31 Bihar Sheikhpura\n32 Himachal Pradesh Lahul and Spiti\n33 Jammu And Kashmir Ramban\n34 Manipur Noney\n35\nMeghalaya\nEast Garo Hills\n36 South Garo Hills\n37 North Garo Hills\n38 South West Khasi Hills\n39\nMizoram\nKolasib\n40 Saiha\n41 Serchhip\n42 Hnahthial\n43 Khawzawl\n44 Sikkim North District\n\nAnnexure-II\nState/UT-wise number of persons administered COVID-19 vaccine\n(As on 09th March 2021)\nS.\nNo State/UT\nHCWs FLWs\n45-59 yrs\nwith\ncomorbiditi\nes\nAged 60\nyrs and\nabove\n1st dose 2nd dose 1st dose 2nd\ndose\n1\nAndaman & Nicobar\nIslands 3,772 2,998 5,896 0 21 201\n2 Andhra Pradesh 2,79,665 1,66,228 3,13,353 29,611 20,631 72,756\n3 Arunachal Pradesh 14,866 9,726 19,170 537 1,137 3,038\n4 Assam 1,68,411 58,494 1,85,082 397 3,922 25,393\n5 Bihar 4,11,601 2,18,005 1,89,386 4,078 34,322 1,86,977\n6 Chandigarh 12,240 3,310 12,052 315 788 10,101\n7 Chhattisgarh 2,47,046 1,31,320 1,70,374 2,502 23,469 1,09,027\n8 Dadra and Nagar Haveli 3,722 994 1,820 16 405 1,147\n9 Daman and Diu 1,252 814 1,865 35 156 1,772\n10 Delhi 1,82,322 64,456 2,31,528 7,995 13,773 95,738\n11 Goa 13,806 6,590 8,640 49 1,929 15,787\n12 Gujarat 4,29,991 2,54,597 4,44,510 1,09,354 97,537 6,17,159\n13 Haryana 1,55,929 88,892 78,512 2,917 6,291 65,766\n14 Himachal Pradesh 70,676 48,673 39,910 0 1,064 18,921\n15 Jammu and Kashmir 76,108 24,950 1,98,904 6,256 3,568 55,015\n16 Jharkhand 1,48,452 63,091 1,58,523 11,587 6,151 41,789\n17 Karnataka 4,59,388 2,50,888 1,65,122 1,783 19,293 1,16,721\n18 Kerala 3,69,309 2,03,150 3,30,180 458 9,080 2,17,514\n19 Ladakh 3,694 2,233 8,054 3 305 5,019\n20 Lakshadweep 1,057 843 1,380 11 26 321\n21 Madhya Pradesh 3,69,054 2,41,475 3,09,776 6,904 26,050 2,23,073\n22 Maharashtra 7,32,667 2,72,796 4,47,913 12,968 66,975 4,07,050\n23 Man