    "ls|LS17_S5_U_45": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n45\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 2\nND\n \nFEBRUARY, 2021\n \n \nCLOSURE OF APMCS\n \n \n45. \n \nSHRI Y.S. AVINASH REDDY: \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE   \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state: \n \n \n(a)\n \nwhether\n \nthe Government is of the view to close the Agriculture Produce Market \nCommittees (APMCs) instead of improving and promoting them for betterment of farmers; \n \n \n(b) \n \nif so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor; \n \n \n(c) \n \nwhether the Government has recei\nved any request to review the decision and if so, \nthe details thereof; and \n \n \n(d) \n \nthe stand of the Government in this regard?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n   \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR)\n \n(a) to\n \n(d): No sir. Government has been always supporting the idea of strengthening of \nAgricultural Produce Market Committees (APMCs) and making them more competitive \nthrough improving services and infrastructure. Government has been providing assistance to  \nAPM\nCs for infrastructure and value chain development through various schemes like \nRashtriya Krishi Vikas Yojna \n–\n \nRAFTAAR, Agriculture Market Infrastructure (AMI), National \nAgriculture Market (e\n-\nNAM), Agri. Infrastructure Fund (AIF) and Agriculture Marketing \nI\nnfrastructure Fund (AMIF), etc.\n \n \n*****\n ",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_47": "GOVERNMET{T OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF GOilSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & pUBLtC DISTRIBUTION\nDEPARTMENT OF FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 47\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 2\"d Februaryr2O21\nREDUCTION OF FOOD SUBSIDY BILL\n47. SHRI SISIR KUMAR ADHIKARI:\nWill the Minister of GONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC\nDISTRIBUTION Jc!trtrilr {rFil, srqr gk Trdsfrfi fut{oI d+ be pleased to\nstate:\n(a) whether it is a fact that the Government has massively reduced the\nfood subsidy bill from Rs {.84 lakh crore to Rs {.15 lakh crore in 2O2O-\n2O21 budget which has indirectly impacted the livelihood of the farmersl\n(b) if so, whether FG!, whose share in the food subsidy ball last year was\nRs 1.5{ lakh crore had spent just Rs 75'OOO crore in 2O19-2O2O therein;\nand\n(c) if so, the reasons behind the gap between allocation and actual\nspending during the last five years?\nANSWER\nMINTSTER OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF COilSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD &\nPUBLIC DISTRIBUTION\n(sHRl DANVE RAOSAHEB DADARAO)\n(a) and (b): Food Subsidy is given by the Department of Food and\nPublic Distribut[on to the Food Gorporation of lndia (FCl) and to States\ndirectly in case of Decentralized Procurement (DGP) on the basis of\nquantity of foodgrains procured and distributed under National Food\nSecurity Act (NFSA) and Other Welfare Schemes (OWS). As per budgetary\nallocation provided by Ministry of Finance, Depailment of Food and Public\nDistribution reteases food subsidy to FCI and DGP States.\nAn amount of Rs. {.84 lakh crore food subsidy (Rs. {.51 lakh crore in\nFood subsidy to FGI + Rs. O.33 lakh crore for Food subsidy to DGP States)\nwas provided in BE 2O{9-2O and the same has been reduced to l.l5 lakh\ncrore (Rs. O.78 lakh crore Food subsidy to FGI + Rs. O.37 lakh crore for\nsubsidy to DGP States) an BE2O2O-21.\nOut of the total food subsidy of Rs. {.5{ Iakh Grore in BE 2O{9'20, an\namount of Rs. 75OOO crore only was released as per the directions of\nMinistry of Financ