    "ls|LS17_S5_U_5": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *05 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 02ND FEBRUARY, 2021/ MAGHA 13, 1942 (SAKA) \n \nLOOK OUT CIRCULARS AGAINST FOREIGNERS \n \n†*05. SHRI GOPAL CHINNAYA SHETTY: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has issued Look Out Circulars/Notices (LOCs) \nfor the foreigners living illegally in various parts of the country during the \nlast three years; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether LOCs were also issued in April, 2020; \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(e) the further action taken or proposed to be taken by the Government in \nthis regard? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI NITYANAND RAI) \n(a) to (e) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n\n \n--2-- \n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (e) of THE LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. *05  FOR ANSWER ON 02.02.2021 REGARDING ‘LOOK OUT \nCIRCULARS AGAINST FOREIGNERS’. \n \n(a) & (b)  40,735 LOCs were issued against foreigners during the period \nJanuary, 2018 to December, 2020. Out of these 512 LOCs were issued \nagainst overstaying foreigners. \n \n(c) &(d)  2627 LOCs  were issued against foreigners in the month of April, \n2020.  \n \n(e)  On detection at Immigration Check Posts at the time of departure from \nIndia, the foreign nationals against whom LOCs had been issued, were not \nallowed to leave India till legal proceedings against them were not \ncompleted. \n \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_50": "O.I.H. \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK  SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 50 \n  ANSWERED ON 02.02.2021 \n \nRURAL DEVELOPMENT SCHEME IN CHHATTISGARH \n \n50. SHRI ARUN SAO: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the details of the schemes being implemented b y the Ministry during the last three \nyears; \n(b)  the funds allocated and released by the Govern ment for various schemes during \neach of the last three years and the current year, State-wise and scheme-wise \nincluding Chhattisgarh; \n(c)  whether any proposal has been forwarded to the  Government by the State \nGovernment of Chhattisgarh during the said period; and \n(d)  if so, the details thereof and the action take n by the Government in this regard?  \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR) \n \n(a) The Ministry of Rural Development is implementi ng Mahatma Gandhi National Rural \nEmployment Guarantee Scheme (Mahatma Gandhi NREGS),  Deendayal Antyodaya Yojana – \nNational Rural Livelihoods Mission (DAY-NRLM), Deen  Dayal Upadhayay – Gramin \nKaushalya Yojana (DDU-GKY), Pradhan Mantri Awaas Yo jana – Gramin (PMAY-G), Pradhan \nMantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY), National Social A ssistance Programme (NSAP), Shyama \nPrasad  MukherjI Rurban Mission (SPMRM) and Saansad Adarsh Gram Yojana(SAGY) to bring \nabout overall improvement in the quality of life of  the people in rural areas, strengthening of \nlivelihood opportunities, promoting self-employment , skilling of rural youths, infrastructure \ndevelopment, provision of social assistance and other basic amenities.  \n(b) The funds allocated and released by the Governm ent for various schemes during each of \nthe last three years and the current year, State-wi se including Chhattisgarh and scheme-wise is at \nAnnexure.  Both DDU-GKY and RSETI Schemes are deman d driven schemes and funds are \nallocated to States as per demands against approved  Action Plans. Mahatma Gandhi NREGS is \nalso a demand driven scheme and no separate allocat ion to the State is made . Under the Saansad \nAdarsh Gram Yojana framework, the development of Gr am Panchayats is envisaged through \nconvergence and implementation of existing Governme nt Schemes and Programmes under the \nadministrative control of respective Ministries wit hout allocating additional funds. Under \nSPMRM, funds are being released to the States/ UTs based on fulfilment of certain conditions \nmentioned in the Mission guidelines. \n\n(c) & (d) The proposals received by the Ministry ar e examined as per the guidelines of the \nrespective schemes.  \nThe proposals received from Govt. of Chhattisgarh a nd status of the proposals are as \nunder: \nScheme Proposal Action taken \nMGNREGA  \n \nEnhancement of Labour Budget from \n13.50Cr. persondays to 15.00 Cr persondays \nfor the year 2020-21.  \nAgreed to \n \nMGNREGA Inclusion of wages of “Charwaha” \n(Shepherd) along with the wages of all \nagricultural works under MGNREGA \nUnder Examination \nMGNREGA Provision of Employment of 200 days instead  \nof 100 days in the FY 2020-21 under \nMGNREGA for Chhattisgarh. \nAs per the provision of the \nAct, reply has been sent on \n23.09.2020 \nMGNREGA Inclusion of construction of “Trellis” in \nkitchen garden development work under the \npermissible list of MGNREGA. \nUnder Examination \nMGNREGA Increase of unskilled wage rate under \nMGNREGA for Chhattisgarh. \nUnder Examination \nMGNREGA Release of II nd  Tranche of Central Share \nunder MGNREGA FY 2020-21. \nMinistry has raised \nobservation on this \nproposal. Reply is \nawaited from State \nGovernment of \nChhattisgarh   \nMGNREGA Final Settlement of Cluster Facilitation \nProject (CFT) Chhattisgarh-reg. \nMinistry has raised \nobservation on this \nproposal. Reply is \nawaited from State \nGovernment of \nChhattisgarh   \n \nSPMRM \nFund release proposal for fifteen clusters \nunder SPMRM. \nFunds to the tune of \n    \nRs. 36.00 Cr. were \nreleased. \n \nDDU-GKY \nThe Action Plan Proposal of DDU-GKY for \nthe year 2019-20 to 2021-22. \nAction plan approved \nRSETI \n \nThe Annual Action Plan proposal for Rural \nSelf Employment Training Institutes \n(RSETIs) of Chhattisgarh till 2020-21.  \nAction plan approved \n \n******* \n\nAnnexure \nAnnexure referred in the statement in the reply to part(b) of LokSabha Question No. 50 due \nfor answer on 02.02.2021 regarding Rural Developmen t Scheme in Chhattisgarh and the funds \nallocated and released by the Government Scheme-wis e and state- wise during the last three \nyears and the current year  \n(Rs. in lakh)  \nCentral funds released under Mahatma Gandhi NREGA  \nS. \nNo States/UTs 2017-18 # 2018-19  2019- 20                   2020-21  \n(as on 28.01.21) \n1 Andhra Pradesh 512763  657110.67  720472.46  787347.21  \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 20679.65  19800.64  21020.01  27015.07  \n3 Assam 112366.54  103097.37  168752.49  182510.06  \n4 Bihar 246888.44  281936.01  325093.78  552237.25  \n5 Chhattisgarh 289885.21  289476.07  264031.92  315141.38  \n6 Gujarat 82505.07  102449.67  74758.23  121487.28  \n7 Haryana 30140.64  34829.1  33812.58  58292.44  \n8 Himachal Pradesh 58684.46  75090.72  59748.12  89798.49  \n9 Jammu and Kashmir 125417.69  79334.12  118370.31  85150.78  \n10 Jharkhand 135264.57  149989.63  127292.89  256487.55  \n11 Karnataka 295632.54  297813.1  546271.17  485934.09  \n12 Kerala 185406.4  234048.78  352016.95  333909.11  \n13 Madhya Pradesh 376889.92  452909.74  471894.15  737358.86  \n14 Maharashtra 185828.74  194892.31  167066.42  123455.85  \n15 Manipur 15778.89  28698.66  61074.66  73756.92  \n16 Meghalaya 87060.44  78903.38  102443.59  111543.64  \n17 Mizoram 20081.04  39783.58  52507.57  53983.09  \n18 Nagaland 110492.88  19322.98  33044.7  48382.14  \n19 Odisha 219834.66  216328.3  243278.38  443369.44  \n20 Punjab 61895.86  57826.49  74886.26  98403.99  \n21 Rajas