    "ls|LS17_S5_U_52": "ORIGINAL IN HINDI\nGOVERNIUENT OF INDIA\nMINTSTRY OF GONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & pUBLtc DtsTRtBUTtol{\nDEPARTMENT OF FOOD AND PUBLIG DISTRIBUTION\nFINANGIAL ASSISTANCE FOR SUGARCANE FARMERS\nt52. SHRI PARBATBHAT SAVABHA! pATEL:\nSHRI NARANBHAI KAGHHADIYA:\nWill the minister of CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND pUBLtC\nDIETRIBUTION Jrrtffrr arrd, urc.a gk Trdufr6, fuflq d+ be pteased to state:\n(a) the amount of financial assistance sanctioned by the Govemment for\nsugarcane farmers in terms of crores of rupees during the month of December;\n(b) the framework prepared to transfer the said assistance direct to the\naccounts of the farmersi and\n(c) the numbef of sugarcane farmers likely to be benefited from the said\ndeclsion?\nANSWER\niitNtsTER oF STATE FOR MtNtSTRy OF CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & pUBLtC\nDISTRIBUTION\n(sHRt DANVE RAOSAHEB DADARAO)\n(a): With a view to facilitate export of sugar during the sugar season 2O2O-21\nand thereby improving the liquidity position of sugar mills enabling them to clear\ncane price dues of famers for sugat season 2O2O-21, Central Government has\napproved Rs. 35O0 crores for providing assistance to sugar mills for expenses on\nmarketing costs including handling, upgrading and other processing costs and\ncosts of intemational and anternal transport and freight charges on export of\nsugar.\n(b): ln order to ensure that the assistance is directly credited into the\naccounts of farmers, the sugar mill shall open a separate no-lien account in a\nnationalized bank/cooperative bank and furnish to that bank the list of farmers\nalong with bank accounts detalls and extent of cane price dues payable to the\nfarmers for the sugar season 2O2O-21 and cane price arrears of previous sugar\nseasons, duly certilied by the Cane Gommissioner / Director of Sugar of the state\nconcerned. The bank shall credit the amount of assistance to the famers'\naccounts on behalf of the mills against cane dues payable and subsequent\nbalance, if any, slrall be credited anto mallts account.\n(c): The decision wil! improve the liquidity position of sugar mills and enable\nthem to clear cane plice dues of farmers. There are about 5 crore sugarcane\nfarmers including thear famalies, whach wall be benefited by this dec:sion.\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO, 52\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 2\"a Februaryt 2021",
